**Question:** given a parent with `display: flex`, how do you make children wrap to the next line while each takes exactly 1/3 of the width, all equal?

## The answer

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;          /* without this, children never wrap */
}

.item {
  flex: 0 0 33.3333%;       /* grow: 0, shrink: 0, basis: one third */
  box-sizing: border-box;   /* keep padding/border inside the 33.3333% */
}
```

Three parts, each load-bearing:

- **`flex-wrap: wrap`** — the default is `nowrap`, which is why flex children squash instead of wrapping. This is the whole answer to "how do I make them wrap."
- **`flex: 0 0 33.3333%`** — the shorthand is `flex-grow flex-shrink flex-basis`. Basis sets the size; `grow: 0` stops a lonely last item stretching to fill its row; `shrink: 0` stops items being squeezed below a third.
- **`box-sizing: border-box`** — without it, padding and border are *added* to 33.3333%, so three items exceed 100% and only two fit per row. This is the most common way this breaks.

## With gaps

`gap` occupies real space, so a plain 33.3333% no longer fits three per row. Subtract it:

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 16px;
}

.item {
  /* 3 items per row means 2 gaps to share out */
  flex: 0 0 calc((100% - 2 * 16px) / 3);
}
```

## Why `flex: 1` is the usual mistake

```css
.item { flex: 1; }   /* = flex: 1 1 0% */
```

This distributes space *equally among items on the same line*, which looks right until a row has fewer than three items — then two items become 50% each. Equal-to-each-other is not the same as exactly-one-third.

Similarly `flex: 1 1 33%` allows growth, so the last row stretches to fill.

## Grid does this better

If the requirement is genuinely "a grid of thirds", grid says it more directly:

```css
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 16px;
}
```

`1fr` already accounts for the gaps, so no `calc` and no `box-sizing` concern. Wrapping is implicit — items flow to new rows automatically.

Responsive, without media queries:

```css
grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
```

**Rule of thumb:** flexbox for one-dimensional content that sizes to itself; grid when you're defining the tracks up front. "Exactly three equal columns" is a grid statement.

